       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 30 mg is three times the usual maximum daily dose of 10 mg. Doses that high raise the risk of severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema. Because of its long half-life, the effects can last a long time.\n\nPlease confirm which of these you want:\n1. **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum labeled dose.\n2. **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily**, the usual starting dose. It can be titrated up.\n3. **30 mg was intended.** If so, tell me the clinical rationale, and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it is intentional. A pharmacy review may still flag it.\n\nIf the patient needs more blood pressure control than 10 mg gives, you could add a second agent, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide. That is usually safer than going above the maximum dose. Let me know how you'd like to proceed."
      }
     ],
